{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-categorical-q-connection-unique","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proof","doco:Section"],"label":"prf:categorical-q-connection-unique","kind":"proof","title":"Proof of uniqueness of the categorical $q$-connection","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-categorical-q-connection-unique"],"text":"categorical-q-connection-unique-proof.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prf:categorical-q-connection-unique\"></a><p>The formula\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\nabla_q = q^{-1} \\nabla + (1 - q^{-1}) \\iota_\\xi \\nabla \\circ \\varTheta</code>\nis a fixed <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code>-linear combination of uniquely-determined morphisms.\nUniqueness of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\nabla</code> up to gauge\n(<a href=\"#prop:categorical-connection-unique\" data-at=\"quantum-universes/qu-structures\">uniqueness of categorical connections</a>)\nextends to <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\nabla_q</code> through the linear map; the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-deformation\ndoes not introduce additional gauge freedom.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-q-connection-unique-proof.md","heading":"Proof","page":"b/prf-categorical-q-connection-unique","qa":{"counts":{"pass":54,"fail":0,"warn":1,"na":18,"unknown":0,"stale":0},"milnor":{"total":1,"notPassing":1}}}
